        "p1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Changing tyre size changes the final drive ratio. Going from a 30 inch tyre to a 35 inch tyre changes it by around 17 percent, which can drop the engine out of its power band and hurt performance and fuel economy. To bring it back you change the ratio to suit. If you had 3.07 gears you want a ratio about 17 percent lower, such as 3.55. For more off road performance you might go to a 4.10 or lower.</p>"
